  "_comment": "Biome table for procedural terrain. Each column samples temperature + moisture (domain-warped, 4-octave low-frequency noise) + continentalness. The biome whose climate-cell CENTRE (mid of its temp/moisture ranges) is nearest the column's climate supplies materials. heightScale/heightOffset shape elevation and blend smoothly across biomes (no cliffs). surfaceAlt + surfaceAltChance scatter a second surface material in patches (e.g. a dirty forest floor). flora.spacing = min distance between plants (the slot grid); flora.density = fraction of those slots that fill (0.85 = dense, 0.3 = patchy). Placement is an order-independent local-maxima test so a streamed chunk and a whole region agree. flora.items = weighted pool of vegetation templates (tree_forge.py .voxel output \u2014 see tools/forge_library.json) the decoration pass stamps on the surface. Materials are names from materials.json; templates are names from resources/templates/. Tree 'extremeness' (height + fullness) is selected by WEIGHTING template variants: e.g. tree_oak_lush (tall, dense) for a lush forest vs tree_oak_sparse (short, see-through) for open plains. Variants live in tools/tree_library.json.",
